1
00:00:08,062 --> 00:00:11,862
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

2
00:00:12,969 --> 00:00:17,275
Musa(موسى) was told by Allah, that your people have worship the calf.

3
00:00:17,328 --> 00:00:18,492
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

4
00:00:18,565 --> 00:00:21,543
فَرَجَعَ مُوسَىٰٓ إِلَىٰ قَوْمِهِۦ غَضْبَٰنَ أَسِفًا ۚ

5
00:00:21,770 --> 00:00:26,763
Musa(موسى) went back to his people; angry and upset, and sorry.

6
00:00:27,557 --> 00:00:28,746
He is so sad.

7
00:00:29,119 --> 00:00:34,523
How could this happen in my absence; my people commit Shirk(شرك), and they worship another god besides Allah?

8
00:00:34,883 --> 00:00:36,266
 So angry and upset.

9
00:00:36,806 --> 00:00:38,486
So he went there to meet his people.

10
00:00:39,380 --> 00:00:42,859
What did Musa(موسى) do, as soon as he saw his people worshipping the calf?

11
00:00:43,386 --> 00:00:45,199
He threw the tablets.

12
00:00:45,699 --> 00:00:53,107
Allah has given to Musa(موسى); Al-Alwah(الالواح); the tablets; that had the Huda(هدى) of Allah in them; he had the Awamir(اوامر); the commandments of Allah.

13
00:00:53,734 --> 00:00:59,959
When Musa(موسى) saw, Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) making Sujood(سجود) to the calf; he threw the tablets from his hand.

14
00:01:00,886 --> 00:01:03,042
What would you do if you see somebody throwing the Qur'an?

15
00:01:03,322 --> 00:01:05,294
Something that, it's unacceptable!

16
00:01:06,534 --> 00:01:10,741
But Musa(موسى); when he saw this in front of his eyes, he was in a state of shock.

17
00:01:11,081 --> 00:01:13,154
So those tablets fell from his hand.

18
00:01:14,414 --> 00:01:15,937
Musa(موسى) already knew about it, didn't he?

19
00:01:16,390 --> 00:01:18,304
He already knew about it, because Allah told him.

20
00:01:18,790 --> 00:01:22,447
How come his reaction was different, when he saw it?

21
00:01:23,807 --> 00:01:24,993
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

22
00:01:25,013 --> 00:01:26,847
ليس الخبر كالمعاينة

23
00:01:26,927 --> 00:01:28,936
When you hear something, it's not like seeing it.

24
00:01:30,456 --> 00:01:32,976
Hearing about something is different than seeing it.

25
00:01:33,436 --> 00:01:38,412
When you see something, it's a completely different thing then; when you hear about it.

26
00:01:39,725 --> 00:01:42,574
Musa(موسى) heard about it from Allah, but when he saw it;

27
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:47,133
it was something different and, he was in the state of shock; he threw the tablets from his hand.

28
00:01:47,773 --> 00:01:48,473
And he said;

29
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:54,996
قَالَ يَٰقَوْمِ أَلَمْ يَعِدْكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ وَعْدًا حَسَنًا ۚ

30
00:01:55,321 --> 00:01:59,469
Oh my people! Did not your Lord promise you a fair promise.

31
00:01:59,695 --> 00:02:02,069
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has promised you with victory;

32
00:02:02,216 --> 00:02:04,209
Allah has promised you with the Holy Land;

33
00:02:04,336 --> 00:02:06,115
Allah has promised you with Jannah(جنة);

34
00:02:06,161 --> 00:02:09,935
Allah has promised you with Tamkeen(تَمْكِين); establishment on the earth, if you are believers.

35
00:02:10,108 --> 00:02:13,364
How could you leave all of these promises and commit Shirk(شرك)?

36
00:02:13,887 --> 00:02:16,200
أَلَمْ يَعِدْكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ وَعْدًا حَسَنًا ۚ

37
00:02:16,621 --> 00:02:29,453
أَفَطَالَ عَلَيْكُمُ ٱلْعَهْدُ أَمْ أَرَدتُّمْ أَن يَحِلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ غَضَبٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ فَأَخْلَفْتُم مَّوْعِدِى۝

38
00:02:30,195 --> 00:02:33,153
Did then the promise seem too long in coming?

39
00:02:33,546 --> 00:02:36,178
Do you feel that it's too long in coming, so you gave up?

40
00:02:36,538 --> 00:02:43,294
Or did you desire that wrath should descend from your Lord on you, that you broke your promise to Me.

41
00:02:43,608 --> 00:02:45,574
You have broken your promise to Me.

42
00:02:45,801 --> 00:02:46,281
They said;

43
00:02:46,321 --> 00:02:49,780
قَالُوا مَا أَخْلَفْنَا مَوْعِدَكَ بِمَلْكِنَا

44
00:02:50,906 --> 00:02:56,124
They said; We did not break the promise of our own will.

45
00:02:56,671 --> 00:02:58,058
It is not our own will.

46
00:02:58,731 --> 00:03:01,031
They refuse to admit their guilt.

47
00:03:01,218 --> 00:03:04,307
قَالُوا مَا أَخْلَفْنَا مَوْعِدَكَ بِمَلْكِنَا

48
00:03:04,527 --> 00:03:08,673
They said; We broke not the promise to you of our own will.

49
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:14,926
وَلَٰكِنَّا حُمِّلْنَا أَوْزَارًا مِّن زِينَةِ الْقَوْمِ فَقَذَفْنَاهَا فَكَذَٰلِكَ أَلْقَى السَّامِرِيُّ۝

50
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:21,975
But we were made to carry the weight of the ornaments of the people of Firaun(فرعون);

51
00:03:22,335 --> 00:03:26,778
then we cast them into the fire and that was, what As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ) suggested.

52
00:03:27,464 --> 00:03:30,284
فَأَخْرَجَ لَهُمْ عِجْلًا جَسَدًا لَّهُۥ خُوَارٌ

53
00:03:30,304 --> 00:03:35,167
Then he took out of the fire for them; a statue of a calf, which seemed too low.

54
00:03:36,133 --> 00:03:37,967
Let's analyze; what Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) said?

55
00:03:38,667 --> 00:03:40,752
Musa(موسى) told them; You're broke your promise with me.

56
00:03:41,066 --> 00:03:44,480
They said; No! We did not break our promise with our own will,

57
00:03:45,407 --> 00:03:51,133
but we were carrying with us ornaments and this is the suggestion of As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ).

58
00:03:51,406 --> 00:03:52,402
There are two problems with this;

59
00:03:52,476 --> 00:03:57,198
Number one; they had guilt in their hearts because of this gold.

60
00:03:57,918 --> 00:03:58,842
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says;

61
00:03:58,882 --> 00:04:00,915
First of all, this gold is Halal(حلال) for them now,

62
00:04:01,208 --> 00:04:04,418
because the people of Firaun(فرعون) are the enemies of Allah, and Allah destroy them.

63
00:04:04,565 --> 00:04:07,695
And that Ghanaam(غَنَام) should go to them.

64
00:04:08,038 --> 00:04:10,117
So the gold; they should take it.

65
00:04:11,037 --> 00:04:18,848
They had guilt for carrying that gold with them, but they did not feel any guilt committing Shirk(شرك) against Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

66
00:04:19,414 --> 00:04:22,044
So the scale of Taqwa(تقوى) is upside down.

67
00:04:22,364 --> 00:04:25,407
Taqwa(تقوى) is very small things but no Taqwa(تقوى) in the major issues.

68
00:04:25,674 --> 00:04:31,573
So Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) are feeling the guilt of carrying with them, the gold that belongs to the people of Egypt;

69
00:04:31,713 --> 00:04:36,396
and they have no guilt whatsoever, when they are worshipping a calf besides Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

70
00:04:36,616 --> 00:04:37,902
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

71
00:04:38,009 --> 00:04:48,305
أَفَلَا يَرَوْنَ أَلَّا يَرْجِعُ إِلَيْهِمْ قَوْلًا وَلَا يَمْلِكُ لَهُمْ ضَرًّا وَلَا نَفْعًا۝

72
00:04:48,739 --> 00:04:57,316
Did they not see that, it could not return them a word and that, it had no power either to harm them or to do them any good?

73
00:04:57,876 --> 00:05:01,349
And Haroon عليه السلام; he advise them;

74
00:05:01,389 --> 00:05:09,425
وَلَقَدْ قَالَ لَهُمْ هَٰرُونُ مِن قَبْلُ يَٰقَوْمِ إِنَّمَا فُتِنتُم بِهِۦ ۖ وَإِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنُ فَٱتَّبِعُونِى وَأَطِيععُوٓاْ أَمْرِى۝

75
00:05:09,698 --> 00:05:12,794
And Haroon(هارون) indeed, had said to them beforehand;

76
00:05:12,841 --> 00:05:21,537
Oh my people! You are being tried in this, and verily your Lord is Allah the Most Gracious, so follow me and obey my order.

77
00:05:23,683 --> 00:05:25,070
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

78
00:05:25,290 --> 00:05:34,749
أَفَلَا يَرَوْنَ أَلَّا يَرْجِعُ إِلَيْهِمْ قَوْلًا وَلَا يَمْلِكُ لَهُمْ ضَرًّا وَلَا نَفْعًا۝

79
00:05:35,002 --> 00:05:44,862
Did they not see, that it could not return them a word, and that it had no power either to harm them or to do them good?

80
00:05:46,075 --> 00:05:51,381
Sayidina Haroon عليه السلام was appointed to be the leader over Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) in the absence of Musa(موسى).

81
00:05:51,634 --> 00:06:00,563
وَلَقَدْ قَالَ لَهُمْ هَٰرُونُ مِن قَبْلُ يَٰقَوْمِ إِنَّمَا فُتِنتُم بِهِۦ ۖ

82
00:06:01,057 --> 00:06:08,187
ووَإِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنُ فَٱتَّبِعُونِى وَأَطِيععُوٓاْ أَمْرِى۝

83
00:06:08,694 --> 00:06:12,979
And Haroon(هارون) indeed, had said to his people beforehand;

84
00:06:13,426 --> 00:06:16,526
Oh my people! You are being tried in this.

85
00:06:16,586 --> 00:06:19,368
This is a Fitnah(فِتْنَه); it's a test from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

86
00:06:20,682 --> 00:06:26,831
And verily, your Lord is Allah; the Most Gracious, so follow me and obey my order.

87
00:06:28,844 --> 00:06:34,162
Haroon عليه السلام is telling them; Allah is your Lord, so obey me and follow my order.

88
00:06:34,182 --> 00:06:36,817
I'm the Ameer(أمير), I'm the Khalifah(خليفه) on you.

89
00:06:37,111 --> 00:06:38,484
Because Musa(موسى) told Haroon(هارون);

90
00:06:38,644 --> 00:06:39,891
وَٱخْلُفْنِى فِى قَوْمِى

91
00:06:40,391 --> 00:06:45,530
Be the successor or be the leader on the people in my absence.

92
00:06:45,936 --> 00:06:49,387
So, he appointed Haroon(هارون), and Haroon(هارون) told the people; You have to obey me;

93
00:06:49,561 --> 00:06:52,547
فَٱتَّبِعُونِى وَاتَّبِعُواْ أَمْرِى

94
00:06:52,614 --> 00:07:02,649
But Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); they were already set in there stubbornness to worship the calf.

95
00:07:03,475 --> 00:07:06,455
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! This calf was so attractive to them.

96
00:07:07,002 --> 00:07:08,305
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

97
00:07:08,325 --> 00:07:10,779
وَأُشْرِبُواْ فِى قُلُوبِهِمُ ٱلْعِجْلَ

98
00:07:11,682 --> 00:07:13,742
Their hearts absorbed it.

99
00:07:14,828 --> 00:07:20,237
Even long after the residual of that Ijl(عِجل) is still in their hearts.

100
00:07:20,864 --> 00:07:23,084
This is way after Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

101
00:07:23,250 --> 00:07:25,802
وَأُشْرِبُواْ فِى قُلُوبِهِمُ ٱلْعِجْلَ بِكُفْرِهِمْ ۚ

102
00:07:26,649 --> 00:07:31,263
They absorbed the love of the calf in their hearts because of their Kuffr(كفر).

103
00:07:31,596 --> 00:07:37,069
And Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ); were they loving the calf because of the sounds that was making Khuwar(خوار)

104
00:07:37,303 --> 00:07:39,946
or was it because Al-Ijl(العِجل) was made out of gold?

105
00:07:40,326 --> 00:07:43,835
They said, what was the response to Sayedina Haroon(سيدنا هارون)?

106
00:07:43,875 --> 00:07:51,560
قَالُواْ لَن نَّبْرَحَ عَلَيْهِ عَٰكِفِينَ حَتَّىٰ يَرْجِعَ إِلَيْنَا مُوسَىٰ۝

107
00:07:52,074 --> 00:07:56,480
We will not stop worshipping the calf until, Musa(موسى) comes back.

108
00:07:57,767 --> 00:08:00,085
Do whatever you want! We're not gonna stop worshipping the calf.

109
00:08:01,918 --> 00:08:07,101
Musa(موسى); when he came back and he saw what they were doing;

110
00:08:08,235 --> 00:08:11,348
the first thing he did was; he threw the tablets from his hand.

111
00:08:11,848 --> 00:08:14,135
وَأَلْقَى ٱلْأَلْوَاحَ فِي نُسْخَتِهَا هُدًى

112
00:08:14,301 --> 00:08:17,840
He threw the tablets and in the tablets; was guidance.

113
00:08:18,767 --> 00:08:21,182
And then he rushed towards his brother,

114
00:08:21,729 --> 00:08:27,687
and he grabbed him with his beard in one hand and his head in the other hand, and started pulling him towards him.

115
00:08:29,321 --> 00:08:30,561
 And he told his brother;

116
00:08:30,854 --> 00:08:40,593
قَالَ يَٰهَٰرُونُ مَا مَنَعَكَ إِذْ رَأَيْتَهُمْ ضَلُّوٓاْ۝ أَلَّا تَتَّبِعَنِ ۖ أَفَعَصَيْتَ أَمْرِى۝

117
00:08:40,719 --> 00:08:48,203
Oh Haroon(هارون)! What prevented you when you saw them, going astray, that you followed me not?

118
00:08:48,467 --> 00:08:50,806
Have you then disobeyed my order?

119
00:08:51,726 --> 00:08:54,599
Musa(موسى) said; How come, you didn't come and tell me?

120
00:08:55,613 --> 00:08:59,033
How come, you let this happen and you didn't come and convey this news to me?

121
00:09:00,495 --> 00:09:01,708
Haroon(هارون) said;

122
00:09:02,801 --> 00:09:06,028
قَالَ يَبْنَؤُمَّ لَا تَأْخُذْ بِلِحْيَتِى وَلَا بِرَأْسِىٓ ۖ

123
00:09:06,175 --> 00:09:07,608
Oh son of my mother!

124
00:09:07,928 --> 00:09:13,627
Son of my mother, it means; he's trying to bring up the blood relationship that is between them.

125
00:09:13,814 --> 00:09:15,434
And the mother is the side of mercy.

126
00:09:15,661 --> 00:09:17,467
So he's telling him; we're brothers;

127
00:09:17,521 --> 00:09:18,381
يَبْنَؤُمّ

128
00:09:18,907 --> 00:09:21,039
Oh my brother! Oh son of my mother!

129
00:09:21,339 --> 00:09:24,133
لَا تَأْخُذْ بِلِحْيَتِى وَلَا بِرَأْسِىٓ ۖ

130
00:09:24,479 --> 00:09:29,354
Oh son of my mother! Sees me not by my beard, nor by my head.

131
00:09:30,154 --> 00:09:34,570
إِنِّى خَشِيتُ أَن تَقُولَ فَرَّقْتَ بَيْنَ بَنِىٓ إِسْرَٰٓءِيلَ وَلَمْ تَرْقُبْ قَوْلِى۝

132
00:09:34,930 --> 00:09:38,960
Haroon(هارون) is giving the justification; why he didn't come and tell Musa(موسى) of what is happening?

133
00:09:38,985 --> 00:09:39,738
He said;

134
00:09:39,991 --> 00:09:50,041
Verily, I feared lest you should say; you have caused a division among the children of Israel(اسرائيل), and you have not respected my word.

135
00:09:51,174 --> 00:09:56,093
Haroon(هارون) said that; I would have caused disunity.

136
00:09:56,813 --> 00:10:02,868
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); when Haroon(هارون) told them; not to worship the calf,

137
00:10:04,135 --> 00:10:07,427
they threatened Haroon(هارون), they said; We're gonna kill you.

138
00:10:08,347 --> 00:10:10,920
And Haroon(هارون) said that; in other Ayah(آية), he said;

139
00:10:11,287 --> 00:10:33,557
قَالَ ٱبْنَ أُمَّ إِنَّ ٱلْقَوْمَ ٱسْتَضْعَفُونِى وَكَادُواْ يَقْتُلُونَنِى فَلَا تُشْمِتْ بِىَ ٱلْأَعْدَآءَ

140
00:10:34,193 --> 00:10:39,113
He said; They saw me weak, and they were almost going to kill me.

141
00:10:39,793 --> 00:10:42,146
So don't let the enemy rejoice over us.

142
00:10:43,446 --> 00:10:48,004
Haroon(هارون) was saying; Don't let the enemies because, we have some enemies among these people.

143
00:10:48,051 --> 00:10:49,098
Some of them are enemies.

144
00:10:49,271 --> 00:10:52,104
Don't let them rejoice because of the dispute between me and you.

145
00:10:52,564 --> 00:10:55,487
So, whenever we have a conflict; we should keep it private.

146
00:10:56,087 --> 00:11:04,356
If there's a conflict between the husband and the wife; it should not go out of the bounce of the household unless, it is necessary.

147
00:11:05,856 --> 00:11:07,468
So the problems should be private.

148
00:11:08,355 --> 00:11:12,707
And even, when Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; you bring outside the systems, who did Allah say;

149
00:11:13,241 --> 00:11:15,040
حَكَمًا مِّنْ أَهْلِهِ وَحَكَمًا مِّنْ أَهْلِهَا

150
00:11:15,064 --> 00:11:19,744
Bring a judge from her side of the family and a judge from your side of the family.

151
00:11:19,957 --> 00:11:24,156
If that doesn't work, then you bring somebody from the community as a judge.

152
00:11:24,516 --> 00:11:27,105
The same thing, when we have a dispute as a Muslim ummah(امة),

153
00:11:27,265 --> 00:11:31,665
we should keep it contained, and we should not bring the enemy from outside to solve it.

154
00:11:31,958 --> 00:11:35,011
And when Muawiyyah(معاويه) was having a dispute with Ali(على);

155
00:11:35,997 --> 00:11:39,944
the Romans felt that, this is their opportunity to make a move.

156
00:11:40,791 --> 00:11:44,865
So they started to arrange their army and the news reach to Muawiyyah(معاويه)

157
00:11:44,885 --> 00:11:47,712
because, Muawiyyah(معاويه) is the one who was close to the Roman Empire in the Ash-Sham(ألشَّام).

158
00:11:48,219 --> 00:11:52,501
So Muawiyyah(معاويه) sent a letter to the emperor of the Romans, he said;

159
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:55,747
لا يضرنك خلاف ما ابن عمى

160
00:11:56,274 --> 00:12:01,762
Don't let the dispute between me and my cousin, cause you to be overconfident.

161
00:12:01,869 --> 00:12:06,444
If you do not stop; I'm gonna send you an army that starts here and ends, where you are.

162
00:12:06,844 --> 00:12:08,424
Muawiya(معاويه) is telling them clearly;

163
00:12:08,651 --> 00:12:15,204
Don't think that this dispute between me and my cousin will cause us to open door of opportunity for you to come in.

164
00:12:15,968 --> 00:12:17,808
Haroon(هارون) is telling his brother Musa(موسى);

165
00:12:17,928 --> 00:12:19,148
فَلَا تُشْمِتْ بِىَ ٱلْأَعْدَآءَ

166
00:12:19,195 --> 00:12:21,274
Don't let the enemies rejoice over this.

167
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:23,794
Haroon(هارون) said; They were about to kill me.

168
00:12:23,814 --> 00:12:24,927
ٱسْتَضْعَفُونِى

169
00:12:25,927 --> 00:12:27,576
They saw Haroon(هارون) as weak.

170
00:12:28,896 --> 00:12:36,542
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given every one of these Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء); all of the qualities he needs for this specific purpose that they're gonna fulfill.

171
00:12:37,069 --> 00:12:42,075
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given Musa(موسى) a very strong and powerful personality because

172
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:45,190
he's gonna be dealing with a very stubborn people; Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

173
00:12:45,896 --> 00:12:53,756
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given him a very strong personality, and a strong body, and a strong character, and a strong presence.

174
00:12:54,336 --> 00:12:58,167
When Musa(موسى) was there, they weren't dare to do this thing that, they did in front of Haroon(هارون).

175
00:12:58,967 --> 00:13:06,566
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has given Haroon(هارون) the qualifications; he needs as a wazeer(وزير) and advisor for his brother.

176
00:13:07,559 --> 00:13:09,662
He has given him the ability to speak.

177
00:13:10,519 --> 00:13:11,790
أَفْصَحُ مِنِّي لِسَانًا

178
00:13:11,910 --> 00:13:19,243
Musa(موسى) said; My brother Haroon(هارون) is more eloquent or more clear in his speech to be an assistance for his brother.

179
00:13:19,803 --> 00:13:26,168
Haroon(هارون); when Musa(موسى) was absent, Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) were about to kill him.

180
00:13:26,975 --> 00:13:32,041
So Haroon(هارون) had to calm things down, until his brother would come back.

181
00:13:32,914 --> 00:13:38,334
If he tried to enforce the law and prevent them from worshipping the calf,

182
00:13:38,558 --> 00:13:44,127
that would have caused a rift and a dispute between Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) and the problem could get out of control.

183
00:13:44,247 --> 00:13:46,567
And we know that when you make; نهي عن المنكر

184
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:49,039
You wanna make sure that it will not cause a bigger Munkar(مُنكر).

185
00:13:49,619 --> 00:13:55,475
When you're preventing evil; one of the rules of preventing evil is that, it should not cause a bigger evil.

186
00:13:56,429 --> 00:14:00,055
So Haroon(هارون) is not approving the worshipping of the calf.

187
00:14:00,342 --> 00:14:01,372
He told his people.

188
00:14:01,632 --> 00:14:03,265
See, because he has to make bayyan(بيان).

189
00:14:03,805 --> 00:14:06,404
He cannot be quiet and then say, this is Hikmah(حكمة); No!

190
00:14:06,573 --> 00:14:09,659
He has to tell the people that this is wrong, and he told them that this is wrong.

191
00:14:09,993 --> 00:14:11,961
إِنَّمَا إِلَٰهُكُمُ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنُ

192
00:14:11,994 --> 00:14:13,928
Your Lord is Allah; Al-Rahman(الرحمان).

193
00:14:14,648 --> 00:14:22,274
But he waited until, his brother came back and then, he would leave it in the hands of his brother; Musa(موسى).

194
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:29,938
Musa(موسى) accepted that apology and he accepted the justification of Sayedina Haroon(سيدنا هارون).

195
00:14:30,198 --> 00:14:32,171
So Musa(موسى) said;

196
00:14:32,471 --> 00:14:51,370
قَالَ رَبِّ اغْفِرْ لِي وَلِأَخِي وَأَدْخِلْنَا فِي رَحْمَتِكَ ۖ وَأَنتَ أَرْحَمُ الرَّاحِمِينَ۝

197
00:14:51,650 --> 00:14:59,580
Musa(موسى) said; Oh Allah! Forgive me and my brother, and include us both in your mercy, because you are the Most Merciful.

198
00:14:59,930 --> 00:15:02,430
Musa(موسى) had a very soft and merciful heart.

199
00:15:03,344 --> 00:15:05,651
Even though, he was in a moment of anger;

200
00:15:06,304 --> 00:15:10,311
he was very angry and he was grabbing his brother by his beard and by his head.

201
00:15:10,751 --> 00:15:17,818
But immediately, when he saw that his brother was on the right side, he started making Dua(دُعَا) for him and his brother.

202
00:15:19,471 --> 00:15:23,634
And this shows the love of following the truth.

203
00:15:23,794 --> 00:15:25,613
It is not stubbornness.

204
00:15:25,639 --> 00:15:30,406
We don't follow our desires; we follow the Haqq(حَقّ) wherever it is.

205
00:15:30,746 --> 00:15:34,593
So Musa(موسى) in the beginning, he saw that this was a mistake, so he came to stop it.

206
00:15:34,788 --> 00:15:37,062
And then when the explanation was given to him,

207
00:15:37,202 --> 00:15:42,132
he knew that his brother was doing the right thing, so he immediately made Dua(دُعَا) for his brother.

208
00:15:43,271 --> 00:15:50,121
And then Musa(موسى) turned towards As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ); the cause of all of this problem.

209
00:15:50,375 --> 00:15:50,775
He said;

210
00:15:50,841 --> 00:15:53,421
قَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكَ يَا سَامِرِيُّ۝

211
00:15:53,748 --> 00:15:56,803
And what is the matter with you; Oh Samiri(سَّامِرِيُّ)?

212
00:15:57,063 --> 00:16:01,710
Musa(موسى); when he first came, Who did he first blame?

213
00:16:02,083 --> 00:16:04,605
First; he directed the blame to his people.

214
00:16:05,292 --> 00:16:06,825
And then who did he blame next?

215
00:16:07,565 --> 00:16:08,465
Haroon(هارون)!

216
00:16:09,172 --> 00:16:11,634
Finally, he blamed As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ).

217
00:16:11,754 --> 00:16:13,588
Even though, As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ) was the cause of the problem.

218
00:16:13,794 --> 00:16:15,028
Look at the Hikmah(حكمة) in that.

219
00:16:15,921 --> 00:16:21,868
Who is the one who's responsible for this sin; it is the whole people,

220
00:16:21,893 --> 00:16:27,998
 because see, As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ); if he gave this advice and that people didn't follow it; it wouldn't have occurred.

221
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:32,469
Always in every ummah(امة) they are going to be some people who will call to evil.

222
00:16:33,109 --> 00:16:35,163
Now, is the ummah(امة) going to follow them or not?

223
00:16:35,729 --> 00:16:37,463
So who carries the burden?

224
00:16:37,669 --> 00:16:38,773
It is the ummah(امة).

225
00:16:39,935 --> 00:16:42,655
It is the whole ummah(امة) of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

226
00:16:42,815 --> 00:16:45,676
So Musa(موسى) directed the blame to them first.

227
00:16:46,149 --> 00:16:47,029
أَخْلَفْتُم مَّوْعِدِى۝

228
00:16:47,049 --> 00:16:47,973
He said;

229
00:16:48,309 --> 00:16:53,255
أَفَطَالَ عَلَيْكُمُ ٱلْعَهْدُ أَمْ أَرَدتُّمْ أَن يَحِلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ غَضَبٌ مِّن رَّبِّكُمْ فَأَخْلَفْتُم مَّوْعِدِى۝

230
00:16:53,377 --> 00:16:56,108
Do you want the anger of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to come on you.

231
00:16:56,302 --> 00:16:59,158
So he first blame the ummah(امة) of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

232
00:16:59,291 --> 00:17:05,923
Because if they did not follow the advice; this problem would have stopped right there, and it wouldn't have occurred.

233
00:17:07,123 --> 00:17:09,903
So in the beginning, it's the responsibility of the ummah(امة).

234
00:17:10,443 --> 00:17:14,930
Any problem that we are going through today; it is our problem; the problem of the ummah(امة).

235
00:17:16,123 --> 00:17:24,395
The problem that is happening in Iraq(عراق) or in Chechnya or in Kashmir(كشمير) or in Falastine(فلسطين) or in As-Somal(اسومال) or in Eritrea or any part of the Muslim world or in Sudan.

236
00:17:24,501 --> 00:17:27,200
It is our problem collectively as an ummah(امة).

237
00:17:27,787 --> 00:17:31,304
And then who does the blame go to next?

238
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:32,567
The leaders!

239
00:17:33,220 --> 00:17:35,167
Musa(موسى) did not go and talk to As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ) next,

240
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:38,812
he went to the Ameer(أمير); he went to the leader; he went to his brother; Haroon(هارون).

241
00:17:38,979 --> 00:17:48,625
قَالَ يَٰهَٰرُونُ مَا مَنَعَكَ إِذْ رَأَيْتَهُمْ ضَلُّوٓاْ۝ أَلَّا تَتَّبِعَنِ ۖ أَفَعَصَيْتَ أَمْرِى۝

242
00:17:48,731 --> 00:17:51,058
How come he didn't convey this message to me?

243
00:17:51,358 --> 00:17:54,720
You are the leader, you are held responsible, you are held accountable.

244
00:17:56,193 --> 00:18:02,352
And then in the end, Musa(موسى) went to As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ) and told him; what's wrong with you As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ)?

245
00:18:03,332 --> 00:18:06,954
Because As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ); he's following Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ), and he's only one person.

246
00:18:08,134 --> 00:18:12,502
If the people and the leader stand against him; he couldn't do anything.

247
00:18:13,729 --> 00:18:15,809
قَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكَ يَا سَامِرِيُّ۝

248
00:18:15,829 --> 00:18:18,409
And what is the matter with you; Oh Samiri(سَّامِرِيُّ)?

249
00:18:19,303 --> 00:18:24,429
فَقَبَضْتُ قَبْضَةً مِّنْ أَثَرِ ٱلرَّسُولِ فَنَبَذْتُهَا وَكَذَٰلِكَ سَوَّلَتْ لِى نَفْسِى۝

250
00:18:25,049 --> 00:18:35,258
I saw what they saw not, so I took a hand full of dust from the hoof print of the messenger; Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل), and I threw it into the fire.

251
00:18:35,898 --> 00:18:38,021
Thus my inner self suggested to me.

252
00:18:38,148 --> 00:18:39,807
And we talked about how he did this.

253
00:18:40,293 --> 00:18:46,242
When Allahسُبحانه وتعالى was drowning Firaun(فرعون) and his army; Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) was there.

254
00:18:47,455 --> 00:18:54,622
As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ) was able; through an Ayah(آية); sign of Allah; something supernatural; was able to see Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل),

255
00:18:54,935 --> 00:18:58,489
and was able to see the footsteps of Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) or the horse of Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل).

256
00:18:59,769 --> 00:19:01,771
And he was picking up from that dirt.

257
00:19:02,605 --> 00:19:07,847
And then he mixed it with the gold, which the woman of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) had;

258
00:19:07,920 --> 00:19:09,280
and that gold belong to who?

259
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:10,405
To the woman of Egypt.

260
00:19:11,292 --> 00:19:13,928
They mixed it together and they made the calf.

261
00:19:14,401 --> 00:19:18,554
That calf started making some strange sounds like, a sound of a calf.

262
00:19:18,921 --> 00:19:20,553
So they started worshipping it.

263
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:28,665
Musa(موسى) made his decision in terms of the punishment to As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ);

264
00:19:28,685 --> 00:19:30,915
he handed down the punishment to As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ).

265
00:19:31,201 --> 00:19:34,641
And that is that, As-Samiri(السَّامِرِيُّ) be exiled for the rest of his life.

266
00:19:36,130 --> 00:19:39,310
Because of this sin, you cannot be part of our ummah(امة) anymore.

267
00:19:39,330 --> 00:19:41,753
You have to leave us alone and we will leave you alone.

268
00:19:42,659 --> 00:19:43,673
Musa(موسى) here is saying;

269
00:19:43,726 --> 00:19:51,325
قَالَ فَاذْهَبْ فَإِنَّ لَكَ فِي الْحَيَاةِ أَن تَقُولَ لَا مِسَاسَ ۖ

270
00:19:51,452 --> 00:19:52,290
Musa(موسى) said;

271
00:19:52,323 --> 00:20:03,702
Then go away, and verily your punishment in this life will be, that you will say touch me not; you have a promise that will not fail.

272
00:20:04,589 --> 00:20:09,156
قَالَ فَاذْهَبْ فَإِنَّ لَكَ فِي الْحَيَاةِ أَن تَقُولَ لَا مِسَاسَ ۖ وَإِنَّ لَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَّن تُخْلَفَهُ ۖ

273
00:20:09,242 --> 00:20:10,336
Musa(موسى); In other word is saying;

274
00:20:10,383 --> 00:20:14,216
Go! In this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) you will not be with us, and we will not touch you.

275
00:20:14,523 --> 00:20:15,198
And then he said;

276
00:20:15,298 --> 00:20:16,965
إِنَّ لَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَّن تُخْلَفَهُ ۖ

277
00:20:17,426 --> 00:20:20,478
We're gonna leave you now, alone; This is a punishment in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا)

278
00:20:20,625 --> 00:20:25,064
and then in Akhirah(آخرة); there's another punishment that will be on you from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

279
00:20:25,264 --> 00:20:26,624
And then he said;

280
00:20:26,798 --> 00:20:33,757
وَانظُرْ إِلَىٰ إِلَٰهِكَ الَّذِي ظَلْتَ عَلَيْهِ عَاكِفًا ۖ

281
00:20:34,077 --> 00:20:42,179
لَّنُحَرِّقَنَّهُ ثُمَّ لَنَنسِفَنَّهُ فِي الْيَمِّ نَسْفًا۝

282
00:20:42,418 --> 00:20:43,534
Musa(موسى) said;

283
00:20:43,634 --> 00:20:51,161
And look at your God to which you have been devoted; we will certainly burn it and scatter its particles in the sea.

284
00:20:51,897 --> 00:20:53,943
He didn't even want to make use of the gold in it.

285
00:20:54,063 --> 00:20:56,799
He said; we're gonna burn it all, and throw it in the sea.

286
00:20:57,552 --> 00:20:58,625
And then Musa(موسى) said;

287
00:20:58,779 --> 00:21:09,312
إِنَّمَآ إِلَٰهُكُمُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِى لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ۚ وَسِعَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ عِلْمًا۝

288
00:21:09,539 --> 00:21:14,345
Your God is only Allah; He has full knowledge of all things.

289
00:21:14,465 --> 00:21:15,618
It is only Allah;

290
00:21:15,658 --> 00:21:17,165
لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ۚ

291
00:21:17,298 --> 00:21:19,548
None has the right to be worshipped but He;

292
00:21:19,788 --> 00:21:22,334
He has full knowledge of all things.

293
00:21:22,981 --> 00:21:25,244
They asked Allahسُبحانه وتعالى for Tobah(توبة).

294
00:21:25,444 --> 00:21:28,950
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said; I will accept your Tobah(توبة), but there, there is a condition.

295
00:21:29,490 --> 00:21:32,809
This crime is a very grave crime; it's a very big crime.

296
00:21:33,889 --> 00:21:38,333
Therefore, the Tobah(توبة) for it; you have to sacrifice.

297
00:21:39,022 --> 00:21:47,381
وَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوْمِهِۦ يَٰقَوْمِ إِنَّكُمْ ظَلَمْتُمْ أَنفُسَكُم بِٱتِّخَاذِكُمُ ٱلْعِجْلَ فَتُوبُوٓاْ إِلَىٰ بَارِئِكُمْ

298
00:21:48,341 --> 00:21:49,360
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

299
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:57,213
And remember! When Musa(موسى) said to his people; Oh my people! Verily, you have wronged yourselves by worshipping the calf.

300
00:21:57,906 --> 00:22:00,558
So turn in repentance to your Creator.

301
00:22:01,812 --> 00:22:03,252
And what is the repentance?

302
00:22:03,465 --> 00:22:05,292
فَٱقْتُلُوٓاْ أَنفُسَكُمْ

303
00:22:05,396 --> 00:22:06,444
Kill yourselves!

304
00:22:07,584 --> 00:22:11,138
This is a big sin; worshiping the calf is a big sin.

305
00:22:11,724 --> 00:22:14,427
Therefore, they have to pay a price for the Tobah(توبة).

306
00:22:15,807 --> 00:22:21,043
Because Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) kept on changing their mind, every now and then, they commit a crime

307
00:22:21,063 --> 00:22:24,283
and then they say; Oh Allah! forgive us; they commit a crime; Oh Allah! forgive us.

308
00:22:24,422 --> 00:22:30,658
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants them to pay a price, and sacrifice; if they want their Tobah(توبة) to be accepted.

309
00:22:30,711 --> 00:22:31,678
فَٱقْتُلُوٓاْ أَنفُسَكُمْ

310
00:22:31,718 --> 00:22:33,351
Allah says in Qur'an; Kill yourselves!

311
00:22:33,804 --> 00:22:34,684
What does this mean?

312
00:22:34,704 --> 00:22:36,349
The Mufassireen(مفسرين) say, it means

313
00:22:36,722 --> 00:22:45,448
that the ones who did not participate in worshipping the calf; kill the ones who worshipped the calf.

314
00:22:46,195 --> 00:22:48,807
Even if, it is their father or their brother or their son.

315
00:22:49,687 --> 00:22:55,626
And that's why, it's killing yourselves because; you could be killing your father or killing your son or killing your brother's like, killing your own self.

316
00:22:56,213 --> 00:22:59,633
So all of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) had to pay a price even though, not all of them worshipped the calf.

317
00:23:00,686 --> 00:23:03,278
But this happened in front of their eyes and they did not stop it.

318
00:23:04,412 --> 00:23:06,245
So the Tobah(توبة) was; You kill yourselves.

319
00:23:06,852 --> 00:23:12,484
So they took the knives and the swords and they started killing each other and it was a massacre.

320
00:23:12,571 --> 00:23:14,837
It is said; in one day 70,000 were killed.

321
00:23:15,524 --> 00:23:17,967
It was a massacre, blood was flowing.

322
00:23:18,097 --> 00:23:19,119
This was their Tobah(توبة).

323
00:23:19,319 --> 00:23:21,173
Because of the big sin they have committed.

324
00:23:21,453 --> 00:23:24,279
They had to pay a hefty price for this Tobah(توبة).

325
00:23:25,133 --> 00:23:41,656
وإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوْمِهِۦ يَٰقَوْمِ إِنَّكُمْ ظَلَمْتُمْ أَنفُسَكُم بِٱتِّخَاذِكُمُ ٱلْعِجْلَ فَتُوبُوٓاْ اْ إِلَىٰ بَارِئِكُمْ

326
00:23:42,356 --> 00:23:58,269
 فَتُوبُوٓاْ اْ إِلَىٰ بَارِئِكُمْ فَٱقْتُلُوٓاْ أَنفُسَكُمْ ذَٰلِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ عِندَ بَارِئِكُمْ فَتَابَ عَلَيْكُمْ

327
00:23:58,854 --> 00:24:06,171
 ۚإِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلتَّوَّابُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ۝

328
00:24:06,484 --> 00:24:07,154
Allah says;

329
00:24:07,314 --> 00:24:10,348
And remember! When Musa(موسى) said to his people; Oh my people!

330
00:24:10,494 --> 00:24:16,776
Verily, you have wronged yourselves by worshipping the calf so turn in repentance to your Creator and kill yourselves,

331
00:24:17,243 --> 00:24:19,958
that will be better for you with your Creator.

332
00:24:20,165 --> 00:24:21,887
Then He accepted your repentance.

333
00:24:21,927 --> 00:24:29,163
Allah accepted it from them even though, it was Riddah(ردَّة); truly, he is the one who accepts repentance, the Most Merciful.

334
00:24:31,036 --> 00:24:39,894
Musa(موسى) chose 70 men from the elders of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); the most prominent among them; the leaders of the people,

335
00:24:41,187 --> 00:24:48,033
and he took them to the mountain; At-Toor(الطور), to meet with Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

336
00:24:48,106 --> 00:24:55,679
Some of the Mufassireen(مفسرين) say; they went on that mission to apologize to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى for what Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) have done.

337
00:24:56,159 --> 00:25:02,394
So this is a delegation from Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); going to apologize for what Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) have done.

338
00:25:02,701 --> 00:25:07,417
وَاخْتَارَ مُوسَىٰ قَوْمَهُ سَبْعِينَ رَجُلًا لِّمِيقَاتِنَا ۖ

339
00:25:08,070 --> 00:25:15,310
And Musa(موسى) chose out of his people 70 of the best men for our appointed time and place of meeting.

340
00:25:16,010 --> 00:25:17,563
So they went to meet with Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

341
00:25:17,596 --> 00:25:21,869
As I said; some of the Mufassireen(مفسرين)say; they want to apologize for what Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) have done.

342
00:25:22,083 --> 00:25:27,128
When they got there, Musa(موسى) went into a cloud; the mountain was covered in a cloud.

343
00:25:27,215 --> 00:25:28,061
They stayed outside.

344
00:25:28,101 --> 00:25:33,151
Musa(موسى) went into the cloud, and they saw the light in which Musa(موسى) was standing in.

345
00:25:33,397 --> 00:25:35,739
And Musa(موسى) was speaking to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

346
00:25:35,886 --> 00:25:37,033
And then, Musa(موسى) came out.

347
00:25:37,253 --> 00:25:42,665
When Musa(موسى) came out, these men; the best of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل), they said;

348
00:25:42,819 --> 00:25:59,868
وَإِذْ قُلْتُمْ يَٰمُوسَىٰ لَن نُّؤْمِنَ لَكَ حَتَّىٰ نَرَى ٱللَّهَ جَهْرَةً فَأأَخَذَتْكُمُ ٱلصَّٰعِقَةُ وَأَنتُمْ تَنظُرُونَ۝

349
00:26:00,201 --> 00:26:03,473
Oh Musa(موسى)! We are not gonna believe in Allah until, we see Him with our own eyes.

350
00:26:04,920 --> 00:26:09,060
You come to apologize for the sin and now, you're putting these prerequisites.

351
00:26:10,160 --> 00:26:12,236
لَن نُّؤْمِنَ لَكَ حَتَّىٰ نَرَى ٱللَّهَ جَهْرَةً

352
00:26:12,250 --> 00:26:18,912
We're not gonna believe in your message until, we see Allah with our own eyes.

353
00:26:20,272 --> 00:26:21,999
فَأَخَذَتْهُمُ ٱلرَّجْفَةُ

354
00:26:22,671 --> 00:26:25,378
So the Earth shook, and they all fell dead.

355
00:26:25,725 --> 00:26:27,005
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

356
00:26:27,498 --> 00:26:44,642
وَإِذْ قُلْتُمْ يَٰمُوسَىٰ لَن نُّؤْمِنَ لَكَ حَتَّىٰ نَرَى ٱللَّهَ جَهْرَةً فَأَخَذَتْكُمُ ٱلصَّٰعِقَةُ وَأَنتُمْ تَنظُرُونَ۝

357
00:26:44,710 --> 00:26:48,502
But you were seized with a thunderbolt while, you were looking.

358
00:26:49,002 --> 00:26:53,254
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى sent on them; As-Sa'iqa(اَلصَّٰعِقَةُ); a thunderbolt; it killed them all.

359
00:26:54,014 --> 00:26:54,634
Allahu Akbar(الله اكبر)!

360
00:26:54,654 --> 00:26:57,352
Now, Musa(موسى) is in a dilemma.

361
00:26:58,425 --> 00:27:04,822
Musa(موسى) took these 70, which are the best of the Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) to go and to apologize to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

362
00:27:06,047 --> 00:27:07,320
These 70 are dead.

363
00:27:08,680 --> 00:27:10,749
What will Musa(موسى) tell the people when he goes back?

364
00:27:11,349 --> 00:27:12,689
The people will completely lose hope.

365
00:27:12,749 --> 00:27:15,889
If these are the best of us and this is, what happened to them; We have no hope.

366
00:27:17,109 --> 00:27:23,031
So Musa(موسى) knew that his people are going to be in; Halat-e-Ya's(حالتِ يأس); despair.

367
00:27:23,718 --> 00:27:28,464
These are the best among us, these are the ones whom we expect Allah to accept their apology.

368
00:27:28,778 --> 00:27:33,900
If Allah did not accept their apology, and Allah killed them all, what will happen to us?

369
00:27:34,967 --> 00:27:37,813
Musaعليه السلام said;

370
00:27:38,140 --> 00:27:54,279
فَلَمَّا أَخَذَتْهُمُ الرَّجْفَةُ قَالَ رَبِّ لَوْ شِئْتَ أَهْلَكْتَهُم مِّن قَبْلُ وَإِيَّايَ ۖ

371
00:27:54,759 --> 00:27:59,952
Oh Allah! If it had been your will, you could have destroyed them, and me before.

372
00:28:00,058 --> 00:28:02,425
Allah! If you wanted, you could have destroyed us before.

373
00:28:02,698 --> 00:28:11,244
أَتُهْلِكُنَا بِمَا فَعَلَ السُّفَهَاءُ مِنَّا ۖ

374
00:28:11,597 --> 00:28:15,885
Would you destroy us for the deeds of the foolish ones among us?

375
00:28:15,938 --> 00:28:19,692
There are some among us, who are foolish; Are you going to destroy us all because of them.

376
00:28:19,938 --> 00:28:34,114
إِنْ هِيَ إِلَّا فِتْنَتُكَ تُضِلُّ بِهَا مَن تَشَاءُ وَتَهْدِي مَن تَشَاءُ ۖ

377
00:28:34,614 --> 00:28:47,344
أَنتَ وَلِيُّنَا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا ۖ وَأَنتَ خَيْرُ الْغَافِرِينَ۝

378
00:28:47,509 --> 00:28:54,854
It is only your trial by which you lead astray whom You will, and You keep guided whom You will; You are our protector.

379
00:28:54,894 --> 00:28:59,580
So, forgive us and have mercy on us; You are the best of those who forgive.

380
00:28:59,813 --> 00:29:00,640
And then he said;

381
00:29:00,746 --> 00:29:05,735
وَاكْتُبْ لَنَا فِي هَٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ إِنَّا هُدْنَا إِلَيْكَ ۚ

382
00:29:06,171 --> 00:29:11,452
And ordained for us good in this world and in the hereafter, certainly we have turned on to You.

383
00:29:12,305 --> 00:29:13,648
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى said;

384
00:29:13,838 --> 00:29:17,012
قَالَ عَذَابِي أُصِيبُ بِهِ مَنْ أَشَاءُ ۖ

385
00:29:17,438 --> 00:29:21,530
My punishment I afflict there with whom I will.

386
00:29:21,597 --> 00:29:23,930
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى can punish whomever, He wills.

387
00:29:24,270 --> 00:29:26,749
وَرَحْمَتِي وَسِعَتْ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ ۚ

388
00:29:27,435 --> 00:29:30,889
And My mercy embraces all things.

389
00:29:31,455 --> 00:29:33,829
The mercy of Allah embraces all things.

390
00:29:34,422 --> 00:29:49,223
فَسَأَكْتُبُهَا لِلَّذِينَ يَتَّقُونَ وَيُؤْتُونَ الزَّكَاةَ وَالَّذِينَ هُم بِآيَاتِنَا يُؤْمِنُونَ۝

391
00:29:49,695 --> 00:29:54,994
That mercy; I shall ordain for those who are Muttaqi(مُتَّقى); righteous, and give Zakah(زكوة),

392
00:29:55,247 --> 00:29:58,487
and the ones who believe in our Ayaat(آيات), who are they?

393
00:29:59,687 --> 00:30:07,417
الَّذِينَ يَتَّبِعُونَ الرَّسُولَ النَّبِيَّ الْأُمِّيَّ الَّذِي يَجِدُونَهُ مَكْتُوبًا عِندَهُمْ فِي التَّوْرَاةِ وَالْإِنجِيلِ

394
00:30:08,435 --> 00:30:09,533
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

395
00:30:09,553 --> 00:30:18,555
Those who follow the messenger; the prophet who can neither read nor write, whom they find written with them in the Taurat(تورات) and the Injeel(انجيل).

396
00:30:19,035 --> 00:30:25,671
The Bisharah(بشارة); the glad tidings of Syedina Muhammadﷺ was given to Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) in that moment.

397
00:30:25,857 --> 00:30:26,671
Where is it?

398
00:30:27,964 --> 00:30:31,144
They hid it; they changed it; they altered it.

399
00:30:32,077 --> 00:30:39,296
But the promise of Rasool Allah ﷺ was given to Musa(موسى) and this honour was given to Rasool Allah ﷺ in that time,

400
00:30:39,563 --> 00:30:41,749
in the presence of the leaders of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

401
00:30:42,303 --> 00:30:43,265
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

402
00:30:43,305 --> 00:30:47,852
ثُمَّ بَعَثْنَاكُم مِّن بَعْدِ مَوْتِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ۝

403
00:30:48,378 --> 00:30:53,004
Then We raised you up after your death so that, you may be grateful.

404
00:30:53,224 --> 00:30:56,078
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى raised them up after their death.

405
00:30:57,344 --> 00:31:01,798
Musa(موسى); he brought them; the laws of Allah, and he said; Follow them.

406
00:31:02,398 --> 00:31:05,791
This is the law of Allah; you have to follow it; Give me your promise that, you will follow it.

407
00:31:06,184 --> 00:31:12,024
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) said; No! show us what is in there first, and then we're gonna tell you, are we gonna follow it or not.

408
00:31:12,537 --> 00:31:17,126
This is coming from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and they know that it is the word of Allah.

409
00:31:17,300 --> 00:31:21,865
They told Musa(موسى); we're not gonna follow it until, you let us know what is written there.

410
00:31:22,578 --> 00:31:24,432
Show us what is there first.

411
00:31:25,512 --> 00:31:27,165
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

412
00:31:27,585 --> 00:31:31,594
وَإِذْ أَخَذْنَا مِيثَٰقَكُمْ وَرَفَعْنَا فَوْقَكُمُ ٱلطُّورَ

413
00:31:31,847 --> 00:31:36,335
And remember, when We took your covenant, and We raised above you the mountain.

414
00:31:37,748 --> 00:31:41,871
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى lifted up a mountain in the air,

415
00:31:42,804 --> 00:31:49,920
and this mountain flew over Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل), and is stopped right there, like a cloud over their heads.

416
00:31:51,127 --> 00:31:53,673
And then, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل);

417
00:31:54,220 --> 00:31:59,899
You either follow the word of Allah otherwise, this mountain will crush you.

418
00:32:01,126 --> 00:32:02,606
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

419
00:32:02,846 --> 00:32:25,009
وَإِذْ نَتَقْنَا ٱلْجَبَلَ فَوْقَهُمْ كَأَنَّهُۥ ظُلَّةٌ وَظَنُّوٓاْ أَنَّهُۥ وَاقِعٌۢ بِهِمْ خُذُواْ مَآ ءَاتَيْنَٰكُم بِقُوَّةٍۢ

420
00:32:25,416 --> 00:32:40,436
 خُذُواْ مَآ ءَاتَيْنَٰكُم بِقُوَّةٍۢ وَٱذْكُكُرُواْ مَا فِيهِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ۝

421
00:32:40,524 --> 00:32:45,256
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; And We raised the mountain above your heads as, if it is a canopy.

422
00:32:47,036 --> 00:32:54,440
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told them; You either follow the word of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى otherwise, you will be crushed under this mountain.

423
00:32:55,087 --> 00:33:00,023
And Mufassireen(مفسرين) say; that Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); as soon as they saw the mountain above their heads,

424
00:33:00,063 --> 00:33:02,419
they said; We're gonna follow, fine; we agree.

425
00:33:02,979 --> 00:33:05,149
And they made Sujood(سجود).

426
00:33:05,169 --> 00:33:06,314
Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) says;

427
00:33:06,600 --> 00:33:09,607
They didn't make the Sujood(سجود) on their forehead and on their nose;

428
00:33:09,767 --> 00:33:14,349
they made Sujood(سجود) on their cheeks so that they can look with one eye up to the mountain.

429
00:33:14,869 --> 00:33:18,263
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is giving Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) many chances.

430
00:33:19,075 --> 00:33:26,264
An incident happened where, one old man from Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) was killed.

431
00:33:26,638 --> 00:33:27,911
This man was wealthy.

432
00:33:28,724 --> 00:33:30,204
They couldn't find out who killed him.

433
00:33:30,978 --> 00:33:32,807
They didn't know; they tried; they searched.

434
00:33:33,607 --> 00:33:37,350
Nobody admitted to the crime and they looked around; they didn't know who killed him.

435
00:33:38,620 --> 00:33:42,393
So they went to Musa(موسى) and they said; Oh Musa(موسى)! We wanted to solve this crime.

436
00:33:44,253 --> 00:33:49,685
Somebody is killed; We don't know who killed him; Solve it for us.

437
00:33:51,232 --> 00:33:54,754
So Musa(موسى) asked Allahسُبحانه وتعالى for a solution to this problem.

438
00:33:55,287 --> 00:33:57,434
Musa(موسى) went to Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) and said;

439
00:33:57,927 --> 00:34:02,159
وَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوْمِهِۦٓ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَأْمُرُكُمْ أَن تَذْبَحُواْ بَقَرَةً ۖ

440
00:34:02,826 --> 00:34:08,139
Musa(موسى) went to his people and said; Allah is commanding you to sacrifice a cow.

441
00:34:09,992 --> 00:34:13,096
They said; What are you making fun of us; Are you joking with us?

442
00:34:13,609 --> 00:34:18,221
We're asking you to solve a crime of somebody who was killed, and you're telling us to kill a cow.

443
00:34:18,448 --> 00:34:19,361
What are you talking about?

444
00:34:20,795 --> 00:34:21,555
They said;

445
00:34:22,248 --> 00:34:28,406
وَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوْمِهِۦٓ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَأْمُرُكُمْ أَن تَذْبَحُواْ بَقَرَةً ۖ قَالُوٓاْ أَتَتَّخِذُنَا هُزُوًا ۖ

446
00:34:28,946 --> 00:34:31,812
They said; Do you make fun of us?

447
00:34:33,599 --> 00:34:34,772
What did Musa(موسى) say?

448
00:34:35,199 --> 00:34:36,705
إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَأْمُرُكُمْ

449
00:34:36,745 --> 00:34:38,164
Allah is commending you.

450
00:34:39,971 --> 00:34:42,584
And Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) said; that you making fun of us, are you joking?

451
00:34:42,771 --> 00:34:45,674
Look at the rude; rudeness of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

452
00:34:45,947 --> 00:34:48,207
What do you mean, Musa(موسى) is joking with the name of Allah?

453
00:34:48,954 --> 00:34:53,037
Musa(موسى) will tell you; go and sacrifice a cow, Allah is telling you to sacrifice a cow, and you go and tell him;

454
00:34:53,077 --> 00:34:54,611
 you're joking, Are you making fun of us?

455
00:34:55,757 --> 00:35:03,297
This is not appropriate for a righteous man to do, let alone a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; a prophet; to use the name of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى in jokes.

456
00:35:04,710 --> 00:35:07,900
But this is; it shows you the manners and the Aadab(آداب) of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

457
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:12,695
قَالُوٓاْ أَتَتَّخِذُنَا هُزُوًا ۖ قَالَ أَعُوذُ بِٱللَّهِ أَنْ أَكُونَ مِنَ ٱلْجَٰهِلِينَ۝

458
00:35:13,084 --> 00:35:16,991
I seek refuge in Allah from being an ignorant or a foolish.

459
00:35:17,084 --> 00:35:19,621
I'm not making fun of you; this is serious.

460
00:35:21,394 --> 00:35:24,210
Allah told them; sacrifice a cow.

461
00:35:24,863 --> 00:35:27,249
Now, if you would follow that order, what does it mean?

462
00:35:27,689 --> 00:35:29,676
You go and take any cow.

463
00:35:31,229 --> 00:35:35,068
But, Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) asked too many questions.

464
00:35:36,268 --> 00:35:37,408
So they went to Musa(موسى) and said;

465
00:35:37,488 --> 00:35:40,844
قالُوا ادْعُ لَنا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّنْ لَنا مَا هِيَ

466
00:35:40,964 --> 00:35:48,873
They said; Call upon your Lord for us, that He may make plain to us what it is.

467
00:35:49,153 --> 00:35:51,053
So they asked a question, they're gonna get an answer.

468
00:35:51,433 --> 00:36:08,233
قالَ إِنَّهُ يَقُولُ إِنَّها بَقَرَةٌ لَا فارِضٌ وَلا بِكْرٌ عَوانٌ بَيْنَ ذلِكَ فَافْعَلُوا مَا تُؤْمَرُونَ۝

469
00:36:08,573 --> 00:36:17,332
Verily, it is a cow neither too old nor too young but, it is between the two conditions; so do, what you are commanded.

470
00:36:17,725 --> 00:36:20,657
So now, their pool of choices narrower.

471
00:36:21,544 --> 00:36:25,250
It has to be middle aged cow, it can't be old; it can't be young.

472
00:36:25,897 --> 00:36:28,420
So they went and they looked at the cows.

473
00:36:28,927 --> 00:36:30,460
And then they came back to Musa(موسى) and said;

474
00:36:30,527 --> 00:36:32,933
قالُوا ادْعُ لَنا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّنْ لَنا مَا لَوْنُها

475
00:36:33,567 --> 00:36:36,487
Oh Musa(موسى)! Can you ask Allah to tell us what colour it is?

476
00:36:37,702 --> 00:36:43,870
قالَ إِنَّهُ يَقُولُ إِنَّها بَقَرَةٌ صَفْراءُ فاقِعٌ لَوْنُها تَسُرُّ النَّاظِرِينَ۝

477
00:36:43,904 --> 00:36:47,814
It is a yellow cow, bright in its colour pleasing the beholders.

478
00:36:47,927 --> 00:36:52,553
Now, it has to be yellow; and yellow is rare, and it has to be pleasing; when you see it, you're pleased.

479
00:36:53,799 --> 00:36:58,075
So now, they're even forced to go into a smaller choice.

480
00:36:58,569 --> 00:37:03,182
Now, the choice is becoming narrower and narrower; the pool of choosing is smaller.

481
00:37:04,182 --> 00:37:07,424
They went and looked around at the cows and then they came back.

482
00:37:07,737 --> 00:37:15,263
قالُوا ادْعُ لَنا رَبَّكَ يُبَيِّنْ لَنا مَا هِيَ إِنَّ الْبَقَرَ تَشابَهَ عَلَيْنا وَإِنَّا إِنْ شاءَ اللَّهُ لَمُهْتَدُونَ۝

483
00:37:15,330 --> 00:37:20,822
They said; Call upon your Lord for us to make plain to us, what it is; to make plain to us, what it is.

484
00:37:21,389 --> 00:37:23,902
And then they said; Verily, to us all cows are alike.

485
00:37:24,002 --> 00:37:26,175
We went and we saw, all the cows; they look the same.

486
00:37:27,175 --> 00:37:28,348
إِنَّ الْبَقَرَ تَشابَهَ عَلَيْنا

487
00:37:28,368 --> 00:37:30,155
All these cows, they look the same to us.

488
00:37:30,515 --> 00:37:33,297
If they look the same; go and take one of them and sacrifice it.

489
00:37:33,344 --> 00:37:35,064
Why do you have to ask all these questions?

490
00:37:35,704 --> 00:37:37,697
They felt that they are asking too many questions.

491
00:37:37,730 --> 00:37:38,817
They knew that, so they said;

492
00:37:38,837 --> 00:37:40,263
وَإِنَّا إِنْ شاءَ اللَّهُ لَمُهْتَدُونَ۝

493
00:37:40,283 --> 00:37:43,109
They said; And In Sha Allah(إنْ شاءالله); we'll find the right one.

494
00:37:44,189 --> 00:37:59,082
قالَ إِنَّهُ يَقُولُ إِنَّها بَقَرَةٌ لَا ذَلُولٌ تُثِيرُ الْأَرْضَ وَلا تَسْقِي الْحَرْثَ مُسَلَّمَةٌ لَا شِيَةَ فِيها

495
00:37:59,469 --> 00:38:01,075
He; Musa(موسى) said;

496
00:38:01,175 --> 00:38:09,434
It is a cow neither trained to till the soil, nor water the fields, sound, having no other color except bright yellow.

497
00:38:09,724 --> 00:38:17,574
So this cow now does not till the Soil, nor water the fields, it is sound, it has no problems with it.

498
00:38:17,867 --> 00:38:21,996
So, these are additional descriptions which are narrowing their choice.

499
00:38:23,003 --> 00:38:30,578
They went around and they found only one cow that fulfills these conditions; only one.

500
00:38:31,172 --> 00:38:37,384
In all of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); only one cow, and it is said that, this cow was owned by an orphan.

501
00:38:38,084 --> 00:38:42,332
Somehow, the orphan knew that Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) want this cow badly.

502
00:38:43,492 --> 00:38:45,858
So he made business out of it.

503
00:38:46,352 --> 00:38:50,021
He knew that there's no cow that has these qualities except this one.

504
00:38:50,461 --> 00:38:52,801
Not only tripling the price.

505
00:38:52,834 --> 00:38:56,883
He said; If you want this cow, you have to pay me its weight in gold.

506
00:38:57,503 --> 00:39:00,003
You have to pay me its weight in gold.

507
00:39:00,776 --> 00:39:02,525
He knows how to make money out of a cow.

508
00:39:03,425 --> 00:39:09,544
And Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) were forced to pay its weight in gold because, that was the only cow that fulfills the conditions.

509
00:39:10,224 --> 00:39:12,078
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

510
00:39:12,771 --> 00:39:14,997
قالُوا الْآنَ جِئْتَ بِالْحَقِّ

511
00:39:15,810 --> 00:39:20,493
When they saw this cow, they said; Now, you have brought us with the truth.

512
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:22,946
They told Musa(موسى); now, you have brought us with the truth.

513
00:39:22,966 --> 00:39:27,739
As if, he was joking or lying to them before it; it shows you, how rude they were with their Nabi(نَبِي).

514
00:39:28,339 --> 00:39:31,014
فَذَبَحُوها وَما كادُوا يَفْعَلُونَ۝

515
00:39:31,087 --> 00:39:32,181
So they slaughtered it.

516
00:39:32,794 --> 00:39:36,014
Though, they were near not to do it; they barely did it.

517
00:39:36,461 --> 00:39:38,867
Why did Allah tell them to slaughter a cow?

518
00:39:38,972 --> 00:39:43,127
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wants to perform an Ayah(آية); miracle in front of their eyes.

519
00:39:44,147 --> 00:39:48,363
وَإِذْ قَتَلْتُمْ نَفْسًا فَادَّارَأْتُمْ فِيهَا ۖ وَاللَّهُ مُخْرِجٌ مَّا كُنتُمْ تَكْتُمُونَ۝

520
00:39:48,383 --> 00:39:52,490
And remember; when you killed a man and fell into dispute among yourselves, as to the crime.

521
00:39:52,663 --> 00:39:54,876
But Allah brought forth that, which you were hiding.

522
00:39:54,996 --> 00:39:56,976
فَقُلْنَا ٱضْرِبُوهُ بِبَعْضِهَا ۚ

523
00:39:57,382 --> 00:40:01,875
So, we said; Strike him; the dead man with a piece of the cow.

524
00:40:02,488 --> 00:40:08,740
Take a piece of that cow which is dead, and strike the dead man with it.

525
00:40:09,047 --> 00:40:10,007
You gonna have life.

526
00:40:10,600 --> 00:40:18,406
So the dead man who was killed; when they touched him with the dead flesh of the cow; the man stood up alive,

527
00:40:18,886 --> 00:40:22,955
and he started to speak, and he said; My nephew is the one who killed me.

528
00:40:24,209 --> 00:40:25,962
Because he killed him for the inheritance.

529
00:40:26,842 --> 00:40:29,884
My nephew is the one who killed me and then, he died again.

530
00:40:30,631 --> 00:40:33,304
It was a miracle of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى. Allah says;

531
00:40:33,784 --> 00:40:44,423
كَذَٰلِكَ يُحْىِ ٱللَّهُ ٱلْمَوْتَىٰ وَيُرِيكُمْ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِللُونَ۝

532
00:40:44,730 --> 00:40:52,409
Thus Allah brings the dead to life, and shows you His Ayaat(آيات); His signs so that, you may understand.

533
00:40:53,243 --> 00:40:54,343
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

534
00:40:54,436 --> 00:40:55,946
ثُمَّ قَسَتْ قُلُوبُكُم

535
00:40:56,126 --> 00:41:02,269
Then, after that; your hearts were hardened, and they are as hard as rocks are even harder.

536
00:41:03,109 --> 00:41:06,906
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! A heart can be harder than rocks.

537
00:41:07,739 --> 00:41:10,156
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; There are some rocks;

538
00:41:10,612 --> 00:41:13,412
وَإِنَّ مِنَ الْحِجَارَةِ لَمَا يَتَفَجَّرُ مِنْهُ الْأَنْهَارُ ۚ

539
00:41:13,572 --> 00:41:17,487
And indeed, there are stones out of which rivers gush forth.

540
00:41:17,973 --> 00:41:21,407
And there are stones where water flows from them.

541
00:41:21,573 --> 00:41:25,243
And there are stones that fall down for fear of Allah.

542
00:41:26,416 --> 00:41:28,296
And your hearts are even worse than stones.

543
00:41:28,843 --> 00:41:30,553
There are stones that can produce water;

544
00:41:30,773 --> 00:41:32,406
there are stones where rivers can come out;

545
00:41:32,573 --> 00:41:34,899
there are stones that would fall down from the Khash'ya(خَشْية) of Allah;

546
00:41:34,965 --> 00:41:39,852
and your hearts are stone; they're producing nothing; they have no Khash'ya(خَشْية) and no fear of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

547
00:41:41,541 --> 00:41:46,197
This lesson of Al-Baqarah(البقرة); a few comments on it.

548
00:41:46,663 --> 00:41:52,975
It is not appropriate to come to the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allah, and ask them too many questions,

549
00:41:53,735 --> 00:41:59,361
that don't have a good purpose behind them or that are not beneficial.

550
00:42:00,668 --> 00:42:06,337
Rasool Allah ﷺ told the people in Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم); this Hadith(حديث) is narrated by Muslim;

551
00:42:06,684 --> 00:42:10,891
أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ قَدْ فَرَضَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْكُمْ الْحَجَّ فَحُجُّوا

552
00:42:11,577 --> 00:42:17,978
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Oh people! Allah has made it mandatory on you to make Hajj(حَجْ); so make Hajj(حَجْ).

553
00:42:19,205 --> 00:42:24,174
One of the men present, it's a clear order from Rasool Allah ﷺ; make Hajj(حَجْ); very clear; doesn't need any explanation.

554
00:42:24,367 --> 00:42:26,180
One man stood up and said; Every year?

555
00:42:26,367 --> 00:42:27,247
أَكَلَّ عَامٍ

556
00:42:27,487 --> 00:42:28,854
Should we make Hajj(حَجْ) every year?

557
00:42:29,180 --> 00:42:30,193
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not answer.

558
00:42:31,053 --> 00:42:32,359
The man stood again and said;

559
00:42:32,406 --> 00:42:32,999
أَكَلَّ عَامٍ

560
00:42:33,039 --> 00:42:34,233
Should we make Hajj(حَجْ) every year?

561
00:42:34,286 --> 00:42:35,333
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not answer.

562
00:42:35,706 --> 00:42:38,814
He stood up a third time and said; Shall we make Hajj(حَجْ); he's insisting.

563
00:42:39,681 --> 00:42:41,421
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

564
00:42:42,014 --> 00:42:45,383
لَوْ قُلْتُ نَعَمْ لَوَجَبَتْ وَلَمَا اسْتَطَعْتُمْ

565
00:42:45,997 --> 00:42:49,950
If I said yes, it would have become mandatory on you, and you would not be able to do it.

566
00:42:50,983 --> 00:42:52,210
Why are you asking the question?

567
00:42:52,817 --> 00:42:59,377
If I said yes, there it would become mandatory on you to make Hajj(حَجْ) every year, and you will not be able to do it.

568
00:42:59,697 --> 00:43:01,995
Why are you bringing difficulty on yourselves?

569
00:43:02,755 --> 00:43:04,315
And then, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

570
00:43:05,035 --> 00:43:12,851
ثم قال : ذروني ما تركتكم فإنما هلك من كان قبلكم بكثرة سؤالهم واختلافهم على أنبيائهم ،

571
00:43:13,291 --> 00:43:17,927
فإذا أمرتكم بشيء فأتوا منه ما استطعتم ، وإذا نهيتكم عن شيء فدعوه

572
00:43:18,727 --> 00:43:23,325
And then, Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Leave me alone, with what I have left you with.

573
00:43:24,018 --> 00:43:32,091
What has destroyed the people before you; is because of there going back and forth to their Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء), and asking them questions.

574
00:43:32,511 --> 00:43:38,087
If I tell you to do something; do the best you can, and if I prevent you from doing something; don't do it.

575
00:43:39,720 --> 00:43:41,014
Don't ask too many questions.

576
00:43:41,540 --> 00:43:44,345
If I tell you to do something; do as much as you can.

577
00:43:44,771 --> 00:43:48,011
Because the orders of Islam are many, and many of them are recommended.

578
00:43:48,164 --> 00:43:49,217
We can't do them all .

579
00:43:49,491 --> 00:43:50,957
So Rasool Allah ﷺ knew that, and he said;

580
00:43:50,977 --> 00:43:51,817
فأتوا منه ما استطعتم

581
00:43:51,864 --> 00:43:53,324
Do as much as you can.

582
00:43:53,831 --> 00:43:57,110
But in the things that are Haram(حرام); you don't do them, period.

583
00:43:57,303 --> 00:43:59,390
فإذا نهيتكم عن شيء فاجتنبوه

584
00:43:59,750 --> 00:44:01,929
If I tell you; not to do something; that Don't do it.

585
00:44:03,862 --> 00:44:07,022
Don't ask too many questions, and this is to the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

586
00:44:07,942 --> 00:44:17,342
Now, this needs to be understood in the right way, does not mean, that you worship Allah on ignorance.

587
00:44:19,182 --> 00:44:21,681
If you don't know something, then you need to ask.

588
00:44:21,887 --> 00:44:27,404
Because, we have a situation which is mentioned in Hadith(حديث); Abi Daud(أبى داؤد);

589
00:44:28,064 --> 00:44:35,496
عن جابر قال: خرجنا في سَفَر فأصاب رجُلا مِنَّا حَجَرٌ فَشَجَّهُ في رأسه، ثم احتلم

590
00:44:36,063 --> 00:44:42,498
Jabir(جابر) says; We were travelling, and there was a man with us who got injured with a stone.

591
00:44:42,518 --> 00:44:46,398
A stone came in his head; rock came and knocked him in his head, and it injured him.

592
00:44:47,205 --> 00:44:49,520
And then he had a wet dream at night.

593
00:44:50,354 --> 00:44:54,027
So when he woke up, he was in Janabah(جنابة), when he woke up in the morning.

594
00:44:54,394 --> 00:44:55,034
He said;

595
00:44:55,287 --> 00:44:57,796
فقال: هل تجدون لي رُخْصَة في التَّيمم؟

596
00:44:58,122 --> 00:45:03,418
Do you find any excuse for me to make Tayammum(تَيَمُّم); is it allowed for me to make Tayammum(تَيَمُّم)?

597
00:45:04,011 --> 00:45:06,038
فقالوا: ما نَجِد لك رُخْصَة

598
00:45:06,851 --> 00:45:09,058
We don't find any excuse for you.

599
00:45:09,298 --> 00:45:10,937
You have to make Ghusl(غُسل).

600
00:45:11,430 --> 00:45:12,557
He said; Can I make Tayammum(تَيَمُّم).

601
00:45:12,582 --> 00:45:13,777
They said; No! you have to make Ghusl(غُسل).

602
00:45:14,037 --> 00:45:14,970
They gave him a Fatwa(فتوى).

603
00:45:15,444 --> 00:45:16,876
وأنت تَقْدِرُ على الماء

604
00:45:17,076 --> 00:45:18,743
And you are able to touch water;

605
00:45:18,863 --> 00:45:20,023
فاغْتَسَل فمات،

606
00:45:20,756 --> 00:45:22,836
He took a shower, and he died.

607
00:45:24,159 --> 00:45:29,369
They told him; We don't find an excuse for you, you have to bath; you're not able to make Tayammum(تَيَمُّم).

608
00:45:29,815 --> 00:45:31,655
So, the news was carried to Rasool Allah ﷺ;

609
00:45:31,702 --> 00:45:36,012
فقال صلى الله عليه وسلم: قال قَتَلُوه قَتَلَهُم الله

610
00:45:37,118 --> 00:45:39,165
ألا سَألُوا إذ لم يعلموا

611
00:45:39,678 --> 00:45:42,138
فإنَّما شِفَاء العِيِّ السؤال،

612
00:45:42,492 --> 00:45:47,887
 إنما كان يَكفيه أن يَتيمَّم ويَعْصِب على جُرحِه خِرقَة،

613
00:45:48,041 --> 00:45:50,941
ثم يمسح عليها، ويَغسل سائر جسده

614
00:45:51,773 --> 00:45:55,241
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; They killed him; may Allah kill them.

615
00:45:56,354 --> 00:46:00,753
They killed him! Why do they ask, if they do not know?

616
00:46:01,013 --> 00:46:03,839
Because the cure of ignorance is asking.

617
00:46:04,293 --> 00:46:05,348
How come they didn't ask?

618
00:46:05,435 --> 00:46:08,655
They did not know, why did they give him a Fatwa(فتوى); and they don't know?

619
00:46:09,795 --> 00:46:10,935
They should ask.

620
00:46:11,308 --> 00:46:12,795
شِفَاء العِيِّ السؤال،

621
00:46:13,055 --> 00:46:16,009
The cure of ignorance is asking.

622
00:46:16,755 --> 00:46:26,466
It is enough for him to make Tayammum(تَيَمُّم), and tie a cloth on his head, and then wash the rest of his body.

623
00:46:26,753 --> 00:46:29,200
But the water; when it hit the injury, it killed him.

624
00:46:30,200 --> 00:46:32,535
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying here; that you need to ask.

625
00:46:32,949 --> 00:46:37,475
And also we learned something important from this Hadith(حديث); Don't give Fatwa(فتوى) if you don't know.

626
00:46:38,002 --> 00:46:43,185
Wallah(والله)! I have brothers coming, and telling me about things that they are told. Unbelievable!

627
00:46:43,805 --> 00:46:45,718
People are giving Fatwa(فتوى) right and left.

628
00:46:45,931 --> 00:46:49,019
May Allah forgive us all, we all make mistakes, all of us, we make mistakes.

629
00:46:49,353 --> 00:46:53,659
But sometimes, there are some of us, and whenever a question is presented, they have an answer.

630
00:46:54,439 --> 00:46:55,669
They have an answer for everything.

631
00:46:55,942 --> 00:46:56,995
They know it all.

632
00:46:57,242 --> 00:46:58,702
Everything, they can answer.

633
00:47:00,222 --> 00:47:04,439
You could answer a question, and you could cause the death of somebody like this.

634
00:47:05,299 --> 00:47:09,285
The Shariah(شريعة) is not a game that you play with.

635
00:47:10,078 --> 00:47:12,105
When you don't know say; Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ).

636
00:47:12,298 --> 00:47:21,201
Somebody travelled from Al-Maghrib(المغرب) or from Andalus; from the extreme west to Al-Imam Maalik(الاِمَام مالِك) in Madinah(مَدِينَه).

637
00:47:21,734 --> 00:47:23,119
He had 40 questions.

638
00:47:24,326 --> 00:47:29,312
He asked Al-Imam Maalik(الاِمَام مالِك), these 40 questions; Al-Imam Maalik(الاِمَام مالِك) answered 34 of them with;

639
00:47:29,332 --> 00:47:29,926
لا اعلم

640
00:47:29,946 --> 00:47:30,572
I don't know;

641
00:47:31,646 --> 00:47:37,275
34 questions out of the 40; 34 he said, I do not know Allah knows best.

642
00:47:38,595 --> 00:47:42,750
The man said; I came all the way from Morocco to hear that you don't know.

643
00:47:43,030 --> 00:47:44,390
Al-Imam Maalik(الاِمَام مالِك) said; I don't know.

644
00:47:46,117 --> 00:47:47,639
This man travelled all the way.

645
00:47:47,865 --> 00:47:52,678
And now, sometimes, we volunteer; we jump into a conversation and we volunteer an answer.

646
00:47:53,571 --> 00:47:54,864
لا اعلم نصف العلم

647
00:47:54,918 --> 00:47:57,744
Some of the Ulama(عُلَمَا) said; I don't know is half of knowledge.

648
00:47:58,438 --> 00:48:02,623
A sign of knowledge is, when you say I don't know; that shows that this person has some knowledge.

649
00:48:03,636 --> 00:48:05,105
They came to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) once,

650
00:48:05,125 --> 00:48:08,685
and we learned two things from this Hadith(حديث) of this incident to the Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

651
00:48:09,179 --> 00:48:11,987
Somebody asked Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) a question when Umar(عُمَر) was a Khalifah(خليفه).

652
00:48:12,934 --> 00:48:14,867
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said; Did this thing happened?

653
00:48:14,920 --> 00:48:15,614
هل وقعت

654
00:48:15,934 --> 00:48:16,980
 The man said; No.

655
00:48:17,213 --> 00:48:25,017
He said; Okay; go back home; when it happens; then come back and ask me, and I will gather the people of Badr(بدر) to give you an answer.

656
00:48:26,924 --> 00:48:29,602
We learned from this Hadith(حديث) of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) that,

657
00:48:29,636 --> 00:48:33,880
we should not try to know about things that we don't need to know about.

658
00:48:34,840 --> 00:48:38,199
If the incident did not happen, why hypothesize?

659
00:48:38,926 --> 00:48:44,299
I mean; there are some outrageous things like, this question that was presented to the Fuqaha(فُقَها).

660
00:48:44,366 --> 00:48:47,834
This is in the old time; this question was presented to the Fuqaha(فُقَها).

661
00:48:47,854 --> 00:48:50,447
They said; What if somebody is carrying wind in the bag?

662
00:48:50,487 --> 00:48:52,375
You know, wind? It comes out from the body.

663
00:48:52,535 --> 00:48:54,525
They said; Somebody gathered that wind in a bag,

664
00:48:54,712 --> 00:48:58,018
and then he put it on his back, and then he flew in the air.

665
00:48:58,038 --> 00:48:59,682
They did not have airplanes in the time.

666
00:49:00,702 --> 00:49:02,208
And then he flew in the air.

667
00:49:03,755 --> 00:49:07,664
Can he pray with that wind on his back?

668
00:49:07,984 --> 00:49:16,198
Look at; this is somebody who has nothing to do, and is laying down on his bed, thinking about these hypothetical situations.

669
00:49:16,645 --> 00:49:18,747
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said; I'm not gonna answer the question.

670
00:49:18,780 --> 00:49:20,514
If it did not happen; I'm not gonna answer it.

671
00:49:20,907 --> 00:49:23,306
Go back home, when it happens, then come back;

672
00:49:23,326 --> 00:49:25,449
and what did Umar(عُمَر) say? He said; I'm not gonna answer it.

673
00:49:25,839 --> 00:49:26,963
جماعت لک أهل البدر

674
00:49:27,176 --> 00:49:34,141
I'm gonna bring the people of Badr(بدر), who are still alive; and make a council; and then we're going to give you a Fatwa(فتوى).

675
00:49:34,541 --> 00:49:36,590
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) cannot give a Fatwa(فتوى) alone.

676
00:49:36,850 --> 00:49:39,890
He has to bring the people of Badr(بدر) to give a Fatwa(فتوى); Allahu Akbar(الله اكبر)!

677
00:49:40,150 --> 00:49:45,502
Now, in the time of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء); they were not supposed to ask some questions because, Wahi(وحى) was still coming down.

678
00:49:46,155 --> 00:49:48,571
Now, you need to ask questions if you don't know.

679
00:49:48,631 --> 00:49:51,158
If you don't know something; ask question. But ask questions about;

680
00:49:51,198 --> 00:49:52,224
العلم الذي ينفع

681
00:49:52,584 --> 00:49:56,090
Ask questions about knowledge that will benefit you. Don't ask about;

682
00:49:56,124 --> 00:49:56,890
علم لا ينفع

683
00:49:57,117 --> 00:49:59,110
Don't ask about knowledge that will not benefit you.

684
00:49:59,350 --> 00:50:00,567
And Rasool Ullah is also saying in the Hadith(حديث);

685
00:50:00,594 --> 00:50:03,794
اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أَسْأَلُكَ عِلْمًا نَافِعًا، وَأَنعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ عِلْمٍ لاَ يَنْفَعُ

686
00:50:04,036 --> 00:50:08,770
I asked You to give me knowledge that will benefit me; and I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit.

687
00:50:09,623 --> 00:50:12,869
Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! If you look at the method of Qur'an; the methodology of Qur'an;

688
00:50:13,669 --> 00:50:18,119
you find that Qur'an does not mention dates; did not mention places.

689
00:50:19,027 --> 00:50:24,092
I mean, there is no historical record in Qur'an, You don't find any dates mentioned whatsoever.

690
00:50:24,906 --> 00:50:25,379
Why?

691
00:50:25,399 --> 00:50:30,962
Because, the dates of when things happen; don't have anything to do with the Hidayah(هداية).

692
00:50:31,889 --> 00:50:36,414
This book; Qur'an; is a book of guidance; So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put the Huda(هدى) in it.

693
00:50:36,981 --> 00:50:40,175
But when you compare it to the Bible; you find that everything in the Bible has dates,

694
00:50:40,195 --> 00:50:47,726
and numbers, and places, and it has the family, the name of the family members of every person that has mentioned in there,

695
00:50:47,906 --> 00:50:50,941
and who they got married to, and their life story.

696
00:50:51,615 --> 00:51:00,226
If you're looking in Qur'an; you find that Qur'an has not even mentioned the stories of the birth of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

697
00:51:00,739 --> 00:51:07,510
It did not give the dates of their birth; it did not even mention the stories of the births of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) with the exception of Eesa(عيسى).

698
00:51:08,177 --> 00:51:08,490
Why?

699
00:51:08,515 --> 00:51:13,360
Because of the importance of the birth of Eesa(عيسى) in guidance.

700
00:51:13,573 --> 00:51:13,886
Why?

701
00:51:13,906 --> 00:51:18,215
Because Eesa(عيسى) was worshipped besides Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

702
00:51:18,382 --> 00:51:18,675
Why?

703
00:51:18,695 --> 00:51:20,148
Because of his miraculous birth.

704
00:51:20,321 --> 00:51:21,661
They said that; He is the Son of God.

705
00:51:21,874 --> 00:51:25,103
That's why, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى talked about the birth of Eesa(عيسى) in Qur'an.

706
00:51:25,356 --> 00:51:27,963
But Allah did not talk about the birth of Muhammadﷺ;

707
00:51:28,170 --> 00:51:35,848
He did not talk about the birth of Saleh(صالح); or Hud(هود); or Ibrahim عليه السّلام; or Nuh(نوح); Allah did not talk about their births.

708
00:51:36,294 --> 00:51:42,125
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى just mentioned; the Bisharah(بِشَارَه); the glide tidings of the birth of Ismail(اِسْماعِيْل), and Is'haq(إسحاق);

709
00:51:42,378 --> 00:51:48,891
because of the miracle in it; because it was to an old man; Ibrahim(اِبْراهِيْم) and an old woman; Sarah(ساره).

710
00:51:49,971 --> 00:51:53,866
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى also talked about the birth of Sayidina Yahya(سيدنا يحيى).

711
00:51:53,993 --> 00:51:55,326
Because of the miracle in it too;

712
00:51:55,346 --> 00:51:57,833
Zakariyya(زَكَرِيا) was old in age, and his wife was old in age.

713
00:51:58,093 --> 00:52:01,292
And a lot after about the creation of Adam(آدَم); which is his birth.

714
00:52:01,625 --> 00:52:04,325
But Allahسُبحانه وتعالى did not talk about the birth of anyone else.

715
00:52:05,572 --> 00:52:10,452
Musa(موسى); Allah talked about the birth of Musa(موسى), because of the miracle; the Ayah(آية) in his birth.

716
00:52:10,806 --> 00:52:14,872
At least, the early parts of his life; there is a miracle in it.

717
00:52:15,792 --> 00:52:23,032
So, we need to concentrate on the knowledge that will benefit; and we should look at the fruits of knowledge.

718
00:52:24,016 --> 00:52:26,289
They came to the Imam Ahmad-Bin-Hanbal(اِمَام اَحْمَدْ بِنْ حنبَلْ) and, they said;

719
00:52:26,676 --> 00:52:29,827
I think they were talking about Bishr al hafi(بشرالحافى) or one of the Ulama(عُلَمَا).

720
00:52:30,380 --> 00:52:35,514
They came to Imam Ahmad-Bin-Hanbal(اِمَام اَحْمَدْ بِنْ حنْبَلْ) and said; He's not a scholar.

721
00:52:35,554 --> 00:52:35,780
Why?

722
00:52:35,800 --> 00:52:38,159
Because he doesn't know a lot of Fiqh(فقه), and he does know a lot of Hadith(حديث).

723
00:52:38,346 --> 00:52:39,499
They said; He's not a scholar.

724
00:52:40,259 --> 00:52:45,006
Imam Ahmad-Bin-Hanbal(اِمَام اَحْمَدْ بِنْ حنْبَلْ) said; He already has the fruit of knowledge.

725
00:52:45,688 --> 00:52:46,155
And that is;

726
00:52:46,175 --> 00:52:47,425
خَشْيَةِ اللهِ عَزَّوجَلْ

727
00:52:47,595 --> 00:52:48,655
The fear of Allah.

728
00:52:50,061 --> 00:52:53,741
You're saying; He doesn't have knowledge, he already has the fruit of knowledge.

729
00:52:53,993 --> 00:52:55,340
And what is the fruit of knowledge?

730
00:52:55,900 --> 00:52:56,660
The fear of Allah.

731
00:52:56,680 --> 00:52:58,693
إِنَّما يَخْشَى اللَّهَ مِنْ عِبادِهِ الْعُلَماءُ

732
00:52:58,906 --> 00:53:01,240
The ones who fear Allah are the scholars.

733
00:53:01,446 --> 00:53:05,286
Now, this man fears Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; so he has the fruit of knowledge.

734
00:53:05,720 --> 00:53:08,139
So we should seek the fruits of knowledge.

735
00:53:08,633 --> 00:53:12,692
And we should study the knowledge that benefits; the knowledge of Huda(هدى); guidance.

736
00:53:13,212 --> 00:53:19,851
And get away from the details, and the minor issues, and the disputable issues, that add nothing or subtract.

737
00:53:19,938 --> 00:53:23,866
And Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! Sometimes, we have big disputes about things,

738
00:53:24,172 --> 00:53:27,572
that are not gonna put you in Jannah(جنة) or put you in hellfire; if you do them or you don't.

739
00:53:28,613 --> 00:53:34,160
Some very, very minor issues, when Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has told us that our unity is a priority.

740
00:53:35,426 --> 00:53:39,847
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّم

